WEBVTT

00:00:00.142 --> 00:00:02.442
Visualization should respect the variable structure.

00:00:02.442 --> 00:00:05.912
Bar charts work well for nominal categories.

00:00:05.912 --> 00:00:11.287
Ordered bars preserve the order of ordinal categories.

00:00:11.287 --> 00:00:13.707
Histograms show the distribution of continuous numeric variables.

00:00:13.707 --> 00:00:19.352
Scatterplots show relationships between two numeric variables.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:25.387
A chart should make the intended comparison easier without adding structure that the data does not contain.

00:00:25.387 --> 00:00:31.797
For example, connecting unordered categories with a line can accidentally imply continuity.

00:00:31.797 --> 00:00:35.987
Connect this idea to an e-commerce team preparing customer, purchase, and web-event data.

00:00:35.987 --> 00:00:43.552
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:43.552 --> 00:00:48.812
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:48.812 --> 00:00:54.347
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:54.347 --> 00:01:00.400
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
